      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at this line, I do not recall why I would want to pull eight pins PE[15:8] high after (or before) the ordinary GPIO setup based on `gpio.inc`.  Most of these pins are declared as \"alternate\" for QSPI, a few are `GPIO_INPUT`, and a single is `GPIO_OUT_HIGH` in `gpio.inc`, so I do not think that this writing to BSRR will have any lasting effect.  Also, it is clearly wrong to use the operator `|\u003d` on a write-only register.  I think this line could be a leftover from early debugging.\n\nSince I cannot document its purpose, I am going to remove it.  If we notice any problems during testing, then hopefully we will have a better idea how to describe the purpose of this line.",
